# [Minimum XOR Path in a Grid](https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-xor-path-in-a-grid/)

## Approach: Dynamic Programming + Bitset

- `dp[i][j][x] = 1` means XOR value `x` is achievable on a path from the top-left cell to cell `(i, j)`.
- Each cell can be reached from the top or left.
- Combine the achievable XOR values from both directions using bitwise OR.
- For each achievable XOR value, XOR it with the current cell's value and mark the resulting XOR as achievable.
- Finally, return the smallest achievable XOR value at the bottom-right cell.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int minCost(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {
        int m = grid.size(), n = grid[0].size();

        vector<vector<bitset<1024>>> dp(m, vector<bitset<1024>>(n));
        dp[0][0][grid[0][0]] = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (i == 0 && j == 0) continue;

                bitset<1024> up, left;

                if (i > 0) up = dp[i - 1][j];
                if (j > 0) left = dp[i][j - 1];

                bitset<1024> combined = up | left;

                for (int x = 0; x < 1024; x++) {
                    if (combined[x]) {
                        int res = grid[i][j] ^ x;
                        dp[i][j][res] = 1;
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        for (int x = 0; x < 1024; x++) {
            if (dp[m - 1][n - 1][x]) return x;
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(m \times n \times 1024)\)
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(m \times n \times 1024)\) bits

Here, \(m\) is the number of rows and \(n\) is the number of columns. The solution assumes all relevant XOR values fit within the range `0–1023`.
